  nonce: 7c7e  # 7c7e
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). CURRENT; anchors and one scope claim corrected.\n- _external_constructor_type (py.py:7431-7440) still checks only `root.id not in module_imports`, with no scope or shadow check; its docstring (7389-7395) records the gap. Pinned test TestDottedModuleConstructorsResolve::test_a_local_shadow_should_not_be_typed is still a strict XFAIL.\n- Repro: import socket; def f(socket, h): s = socket.socket(h); s.send(b\"x\") emits f -> python:socket.socket:0-0:send (type_inferred), and io-boundaries reports net_send: socket.socket.send <- f, a boundary that does not exist.\n- Lazy import def g(h): import socket; ... is typed correctly today. The trap in the discussion is real: _collect_bound_names (py.py:6951) adds Import/ImportFrom names.\n- ANCHORS MOVED: _enclosing_shadow is py.py:5729 (was ~3751), _collect_bound_names 6951 (was ~4928). _external_constructor_module call sites are 6029/6363/6406, plus a direct _external_constructor_type call ~4244.\n- CORRECTION: _enclosing_shadow unions only STRICT enclosing functions (cur = enclosing_func_id.get(caller_id)), not the current function's own params, as the discussion implies.\n- SECOND CONSUMER of the same file-scoped map: the socket.socket(h) call edge itself goes through py.py Case 2b (receiver_name in module_imports, ~8305), equally shadow-blind.\n- Same family, not duplicates: WI-masov (import shadowing a local class, opposite direction), WI-luhah (done, same idea for module_attr_ref), WI-kugap/INV-popup (Go)."  # 7c7e
